---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { ecosystemProfiles } from "../data/ecosystemProfiles";
---

<BaseLayout title="Ecosystem & Standards | Governance Commons" description="A common-ground map of standards, protocols, research, and governance practices relevant to governed AI agent systems.">
  <section class="page-hero ecosystem-hero">
    <img
      class="ecosystem-hero-image"
      src="/assets/governance-ecosystem-network.webp"
      alt="Governance Commons connecting people, documents, decisions, and institutional relationships across a shared network"
      width="1915"
      height="821"
      decoding="async"
      fetchpriority="high"
    />
    <div class="page-title ecosystem-hero-title">
      <p class="eyebrow">Ecosystem &amp; Standards</p>
      <h1>A commons where standards meet.</h1>
      <p class="lede">Governance Commons collects, contextualizes, connects, teaches, warns, and contributes across the wider governance ecosystem. GC is maintainer-led and does not claim authority over the standards it documents.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section white">
    <div class="section-inner">
      <div class="intro-grid">
        <article class="surface"><h2>Collect</h2><p>Bring standards, protocols, research, implementation practices, and evidence into one navigable map.</p></article>
        <article class="surface"><h2>Contextualize</h2><p>Record source, version, date, scope, lifecycle, overlap, differences, and uncertainty.</p></article>
        <article class="surface"><h2>Connect</h2><p>Crosswalk related work without treating different standards or authorities as interchangeable.</p></article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="section-heading">
      <p class="eyebrow">Working relationships</p>
      <h2>Different kinds of relationship, explicitly named.</h2>
      <p>GC may reference, align with, interoperate with, crosswalk, adopt, contribute to, research, warn about, or distinguish external work. These labels describe relationships; they do not grant authority.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="intro-grid">
      <article class="surface"><h3>Standards &amp; protocols</h3><p>NIST, ISO/IEC, W3C, IETF, IEEE, OASIS, AAIF, AGF/AAP, MCP, A2A, and related work can be documented by scope and version.</p></article>
      <article class="surface"><h3>Identity &amp; provenance</h3><p>Credentials, decentralized identifiers, content provenance, attestations, and related evidence systems can be connected to governed-event records.</p></article>
      <article class="surface"><h3>Observability &amp; security</h3><p>Telemetry, traceability, agent security, risk-management, and assurance practices can provide evidence without becoming GC authority.</p></article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section white" id="directory">
    <div class="section-heading"><p class="eyebrow">Explore organizations</p><h2>Explore source-linked ecosystem profiles.</h2><p>These entries explain what each organization offers and where its work may intersect with GC. Detailed verified crosswalks are still in preparation.</p></div>
    <div class="standards-grid">
      {ecosystemProfiles.map((entry) => <article class="surface standard-card"><p class="eyebrow">{entry.type}</p><h3>{entry.name}</h3><p>{entry.offering}</p><p>{entry.relation}</p><a class="text-link" href={`/ecosystem/${entry.slug}`}>Explore profile →</a></article>)}
    </div>
    <p style="margin-top:24px">Next profiles under preparation: IEEE, EU AI Act, IETF, OASIS, and other relevant standards bodies. <a class="text-link" href="/observatory">Explore the proposed AI Systems Observatory →</a></p>
  </section>

  <section class="section tint">
    <div class="section-heading">
      <p class="eyebrow">GC's role</p>
      <h2>Common ground, not a competing authority.</h2>
      <p>External organizations retain authority over their own standards. GC's role is to make relevant work easier to find, understand, compare, verify, and apply while preserving provenance and uncertainty.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="surface notice">
      <strong>Core rule:</strong> No stage may silently impersonate the authority of another.
    </div>
    <div class="actions" style="justify-content:center; margin-top:30px">
      <a class="button ink" href="https://github.com/governancecommons/governance-commons/blob/main/docs/ecosystem/standards-landscape.md">Read the standards landscape</a>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
